===Energy efficiency===

All new housing in Balisca must meet net-zero energy standards, achieved through:

* '''Passive solar design:''' Orientation, shading, and thermal mass optimize natural heating and cooling.
* '''Super-insulation:''' High-performance insulation minimizes heating and cooling needs.
* '''Renewable energy:''' Solar panels, small wind turbines, and geothermal systems provide on-site energy.
* '''Energy monitoring:''' Real-time feedback systems help residents optimize energy use.
* '''District energy systems:''' Many cooperatives share heating and cooling through community-scale systems.

===Accessibility===

The [[Confederal Housing Act of 1974]] (amended 1995) establishes accessibility requirements:

* All ground-floor units must be fully accessible to people with mobility impairments.
* At least 10% of units in any development must be fully accessible.
* All common areas must be accessible.
* Reasonable accommodations must be made for residents with disabilities.
* Universal design principles are encouraged in all new construction.

