===Indigenous housing models===

Indigenous communities maintain distinct housing practices:

* '''[[Wallche]] communities:''' Extended family compounds with traditional construction methods; land held under indigenous title; housing allocated by traditional authorities.
* '''[[Kurupiranga]] communities:''' Large communal houses (malocas) housing multiple families; strong emphasis on communal living; integration with traditional livelihoods.
* '''[[Araucarian]] communities:''' Traditional wooden houses (ruka) with modern adaptations; strong connection to agricultural land; housing as part of broader territorial management.

The [[Indigenous Housing Rights Act of 1995]] protects these practices and provides funding for indigenous-controlled housing programs.

