|-
! Aspect !! Balisca !! Market-based systems
|-
| '''Right to housing''' || Constitutional guarantee || Often not recognized
|-
| '''Homelessness''' || Eliminated as systemic feature || Common in many countries
|-
| '''Speculation''' || Illegal || Common practice
|-
| '''Landlordism''' || Illegal || Dominant model in rentals
|-
| '''Housing as investment''' || Not permitted || Primary driver of housing markets
|-
| '''Affordability''' || Based on cost, not market || Subject to market forces
|-
| '''Security of tenure''' || Strong protections || Variable, often weak
|}

===International recognition===

Balisca's housing model has received international recognition:

* [[Adonian Community]] Award for Housing Innovation (1978)
* Recognition as a model for decommodified housing by housing rights organizations
* Study tours and delegations from countries seeking alternatives to market-based housing
* Academic research on cooperative housing models

===Challenges in international comparison===

Direct comparison with market-based systems is complicated by:

* Different definitions of "ownership" and "rent"
* Absence of market prices in Balisca
* Different measures of housing quality and satisfaction
* The current housing shortage affecting outcome measures

